WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.291
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:17.561 --> 00:20.601
(Kang Hoon, Cho Hyun Chul, Kim Jeong Jin)

3
00:23.271 --> 00:25.671
(Lee E Dam, Moon Hee, Yoon Ga I)

4
00:33.241 --> 00:35.251
(Jeon Bae Soo, Lee Seo Hwan, Oh Eui Sik)

5
00:54.501 --> 00:57.271
(Happy Anding)

6
00:57.271 --> 00:58.941
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

7
00:58.941 --> 01:00.171
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

8
01:00.171 --> 01:01.371
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

9
01:01.371 --> 01:02.571
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

10
01:02.571 --> 01:03.771
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

11
01:04.611 --> 01:05.641
(1 year ago)

12
01:05.681 --> 01:08.481
Mister, could you hurry it up, please?

13
01:13.321 --> 01:14.621
Mister!

14
01:14.721 --> 01:18.221
- Why is this taking so long? - It's all done.

15
01:18.721 --> 01:21.091
- Just rip it off already. - Someone's impatient...

16
01:21.161 --> 01:23.731
There. Eun Young!

17
01:44.251 --> 01:46.051
I rushed over to her place, worried sick.

18
01:46.821 --> 01:47.851
And she...

19
01:50.391 --> 01:52.361
was nowhere to be found.

20
02:02.001 --> 02:03.501
Her time had completely stopped.

21
02:04.941 --> 02:06.501
You love salt bread, don't you?

22
02:07.611 --> 02:10.441
- I don't want it. - Did they move it?

23
02:10.841 --> 02:11.911
Wasn't it right here?

24
02:14.011 --> 02:15.011
Eun Young.

25
02:15.551 --> 02:16.551
What's wrong?

26
02:18.881 --> 02:19.881
Eun Young.

27
02:20.821 --> 02:22.021
What is it, Eun Young? What's wrong?

28
02:28.361 --> 02:29.361
Eun Young.

29
02:29.891 --> 02:30.901
Eun Young!

30
03:00.961 --> 03:01.961
Eun Young!

31
03:18.111 --> 03:20.011
Depression accompanied by panic disorder,

32
03:20.081 --> 03:21.081
social anxiety,

33
03:21.481 --> 03:23.451
commonly known as anthropophobia.

34
03:23.851 --> 03:26.421
If we knew what had happened,

35
03:26.421 --> 03:29.251
we could make a more precise diagnosis,

36
03:29.951 --> 03:32.221
but she has no willingness to undergo counselling.

37
03:33.821 --> 03:34.831
What is it?

38
03:35.931 --> 03:37.031
Why are you being like this?

39
03:37.561 --> 03:38.561
You seriously...

40
03:40.761 --> 03:41.801
Just stay here for a second.

41
03:43.471 --> 03:44.501
Mom.

42
03:46.641 --> 03:48.471
I don't know, she said work is busy.

43
03:50.811 --> 03:53.041
How am I supposed to know?

44
04:02.821 --> 04:03.921
What could...

45
04:04.821 --> 04:06.421
have happened to her?

46
04:16.431 --> 04:17.431
How is it?

47
04:17.571 --> 04:19.471
You look too pretty, it won't work.

48
04:20.201 --> 04:21.741
No way.

49
04:21.771 --> 04:23.441
Unbelievable. Just unbelievable.

50
04:23.511 --> 04:24.511
- Why? - I don't think it'll work.

51
04:24.581 --> 04:25.941
- I'm pretty. - Seriously.

52
04:26.041 --> 04:27.111
You look pretty, so what's wrong?

53
04:27.181 --> 04:28.711
Hey, from behind, it looks pretty convincing.

54
04:28.981 --> 04:30.511
What's so interesting?

55
04:31.481 --> 04:33.721
- Man, this guy, seriously... - They're weird.

56
04:34.421 --> 04:36.221
They do look pretty weird.

57
04:38.261 --> 04:39.261
What's this?

58
04:39.921 --> 04:41.361
You skipped your medicine again.

59
04:42.861 --> 04:45.001
I told you to take it on schedule.

60
04:46.901 --> 04:47.901
Give me your hand.

61
04:53.441 --> 04:57.211
What do you think about what the doctor said earlier?

62
04:57.781 --> 05:00.181
About starting with something small.

63
05:00.981 --> 05:03.251
He said that might help more than medicine.

64
05:05.821 --> 05:07.221
On my way here,

65
05:08.221 --> 05:09.951
you know that intersection?

66
05:10.051 --> 05:11.361
In front of the cafe at the intersection,

67
05:13.291 --> 05:15.631
I saw this posted.

68
05:17.601 --> 05:19.701
It's a neighbourhood cafe, so it isn't crowded.

69
05:20.001 --> 05:22.701
You can try it out and quit if you don't like it.

70
05:23.231 --> 05:24.701
- Walk backward. - What do you think?

71
05:24.771 --> 05:26.901
Walk backward? You're telling a person to walk backward?

72
05:26.971 --> 05:29.441
- Nice. - Walk backward like this.

73
05:30.311 --> 05:32.081
- Walk backward? - Yes.

74
05:32.441 --> 05:34.481
- Man, this guy, seriously... - Look at you.

75
05:34.851 --> 05:38.151
The cups, straws, and sleeves are in the storage room,

76
05:38.221 --> 05:39.721
so you can restock whenever you have time.

77
05:39.781 --> 05:40.821
The storage room is over there.

78
05:40.881 --> 05:42.421
I will teach you the rest as we work.

79
05:42.491 --> 05:43.521
Can I call you Eun Young?

80
05:46.961 --> 05:48.191
Three Iced Americanos just showed up.

81
05:48.461 --> 05:50.791
No chance of closing early today either.

82
05:51.201 --> 05:52.931
Hello, ladies.

83
05:56.131 --> 05:57.131
It is bright.

84
05:57.201 --> 06:00.071
(Cafe Enough)

85
06:01.511 --> 06:03.341
Look, a new lady.

86
06:05.641 --> 06:08.311
The day I first met them at the cafe.

87
06:09.081 --> 06:12.421
- A few labels followed them around. - Did you order?

88
06:12.851 --> 06:16.021
They are a pain in the neck. They are unknown comedians,

89
06:16.091 --> 06:18.791
and they always order just three coffees...

90
06:18.861 --> 06:20.391
and loiter around until closing.

91
06:20.821 --> 06:21.861
So among ourselves,

92
06:21.931 --> 06:23.491
we call them "Three Iced Americanos."

93
06:24.231 --> 06:26.131
It's like a bald guy...

94
06:26.231 --> 06:27.361
Unknown comedians.

95
06:29.031 --> 06:30.071
Three Iced Americanos.

96
06:32.771 --> 06:33.771
Hello.

97
06:34.571 --> 06:38.181
- This... - Well...

98
06:39.111 --> 06:41.681
This is a poster for our show.

99
06:42.381 --> 06:44.681
Would it be all right if we put this up over there?

100
06:44.751 --> 06:46.951
If you hand it to us, we will put it up for you.

101
06:47.421 --> 06:48.851
- Thank you. - Thank you.

102
06:48.951 --> 06:50.721
- Goodbye. - I will be back from the restroom.

103
06:50.921 --> 06:53.661
Come watch us sometime. We will save you good seats.

104
06:53.721 --> 06:55.731
- Okay. - Thank you.

105
06:55.791 --> 06:56.791
- Sure. - Thank you.

106
06:56.861 --> 06:58.931
- You should come watch too. - Please come watch.

107
06:59.361 --> 07:01.071
- Thank you. - Thank you.

108
07:03.771 --> 07:05.501
Put it right here like this...

109
07:05.571 --> 07:06.901
- Sure. - Thank you.

110
07:06.971 --> 07:07.971
Thank you!

111
07:11.811 --> 07:13.281
I am so sick of them.

112
07:14.341 --> 07:16.181
Who would go watch a show with them in it?

113
07:16.881 --> 07:19.121
Exactly. Giving up takes courage too.

114
07:19.151 --> 07:21.151
Why do they keep stubbornly clinging on?

115
07:21.821 --> 07:22.821
Total losers.

116
07:27.021 --> 07:28.591
They were familiar words.

117
07:30.391 --> 07:31.931
Eun Young, we will step out for just a bit.

118
07:56.621 --> 07:57.861
I think it is coming out.

119
07:58.821 --> 07:59.821
Pow.

120
07:59.891 --> 08:01.831
Stop it, seriously. I am not kidding.

121
08:01.961 --> 08:03.061
Hey, I'm feeling it too.

122
08:03.131 --> 08:04.631
- Hey, stop it. - Man, what do we do?

123
08:04.731 --> 08:05.801
Hey, just let me use the restroom.

124
08:15.841 --> 08:17.471
That is it, flex those muscles as much as you can.

125
08:18.011 --> 08:20.941
Smile. Hey, you are good at this. Hey, that look on your face...

126
08:21.011 --> 08:23.151
is not Jim Carrey, it is facial paralysis.

127
08:23.251 --> 08:24.381
Your mouth is completely crooked.

128
08:24.981 --> 08:26.721
How is this any different from his?

129
08:26.781 --> 08:27.791
- Your eyebrows... - No, it is different.

130
08:27.851 --> 08:29.851
Use the muscles right here. No, your mouth...

131
08:30.091 --> 08:33.761
Your mouth should be smiling. Try it. Come on.

132
08:36.791 --> 08:38.201
Show me with your face.

133
08:38.331 --> 08:41.701
Truly foolish, strange people.

134
08:42.371 --> 08:45.171
- You piece of trash. - Hey.

135
08:46.271 --> 08:48.011
- What on earth... - Gosh!

136
08:49.041 --> 08:52.441
Bring it. Hey, bring it over. Hey, bring it here already.

137
08:52.511 --> 08:55.011
No, there is a snake here.

138
08:55.651 --> 08:56.981
Even better.

139
08:57.411 --> 08:59.451
- Even better. - Even better.

140
08:59.721 --> 09:02.051
- It is too simple. - No, it has to be simple...

141
09:02.121 --> 09:04.491
- for the comedy to pop, idiot. - Even better.

142
09:05.061 --> 09:06.261
Even better.

143
09:06.921 --> 09:07.991
Even better.

144
09:08.691 --> 09:11.631
Even better. My girlfriend these days.

145
09:12.331 --> 09:13.501
Every time we meet.

146
09:14.331 --> 09:15.601
Even better.

147
09:17.301 --> 09:19.901
Beat him to a pulp, then bring him back to life.

148
09:22.841 --> 09:24.311
- Next. - Next, all right.

149
09:24.781 --> 09:26.941
- Good. - Around this much.

150
09:27.881 --> 09:31.621
All right, next is Namiko.

151
09:32.951 --> 09:34.991
You know what this is, right? Good!

152
09:34.991 --> 09:37.591
Their constant silliness...

153
09:39.261 --> 09:41.061
puts me at ease.

154
09:45.531 --> 09:49.871
(Asura)

155
09:49.931 --> 09:52.071
How is the part-time job?

156
09:55.511 --> 09:56.511
What is this?

157
09:58.141 --> 09:59.141
What is this?

158
10:02.981 --> 10:05.651
You know those guys in the building opposite?

159
10:08.351 --> 10:09.521
They are comedians.

160
10:10.221 --> 10:11.261
Their name is...

161
10:14.021 --> 10:15.131
Asura.

162
10:15.431 --> 10:16.461
Asura?

163
10:19.101 --> 10:20.801
I think I might have heard of them.

164
10:21.231 --> 10:22.931
They are regulars at the cafe.

165
10:23.601 --> 10:25.401
They say they meet there every day.

166
10:26.541 --> 10:28.441
I do not know what is so funny,

167
10:29.441 --> 10:32.941
but they laugh, bicker,

168
10:35.081 --> 10:36.551
and burst out laughing again.

169
10:39.881 --> 10:41.421
I knew they were strange,

170
10:43.691 --> 10:45.461
but seeing them up close,

171
10:46.221 --> 10:49.231
they are so much stranger.

172
10:52.901 --> 10:54.631
They are really strange people.

173
11:08.851 --> 11:09.881
What?

174
11:10.911 --> 11:12.121
It is fascinating.

175
11:13.521 --> 11:17.721
Do you know it has been forever since you talked that much?

176
11:20.821 --> 11:24.801
Tell me more, okay? What else happened? Tell me.

177
11:25.631 --> 11:26.931
I realised then.

178
11:27.101 --> 11:28.631
The time that had stopped for my sister...

179
11:29.131 --> 11:30.771
was starting to move again, bit by bit.

180
11:30.831 --> 11:32.971
This is a bit spicy. Hold on.

181
11:33.041 --> 11:35.711
It is not spicy. You were eating fine.

182
11:36.111 --> 11:37.141
Eun Young.

183
11:40.241 --> 11:44.251
- No, I know. You go first. - All right, got it. Here we go.

184
11:44.311 --> 11:46.151
- Yes. Let us do it. - Let us do it.

185
11:46.221 --> 11:49.591
One. One, two, three.

186
11:50.191 --> 11:51.461
(Screaming)

187
11:52.861 --> 11:54.421
What made my sister laugh again...

188
11:55.131 --> 11:57.831
was neither that mountain of pills nor me.

189
12:00.361 --> 12:01.501
Hello, ma'am.

190
12:04.501 --> 12:06.001
Three iced Americanos, please.

191
12:06.401 --> 12:08.011
First, take the hit. Then who is next?

192
12:08.541 --> 12:10.511
I will take it. Then who is next?

193
12:10.571 --> 12:12.941
- What are you muttering? - Who was it?

194
12:15.611 --> 12:17.051
- Hey. - Hey.

195
12:19.321 --> 12:20.781
Look down.

196
12:22.191 --> 12:23.521
What do we do? Why is she staring like that?

197
12:23.591 --> 12:26.421
And so, the world's most secretive and quirky...

198
12:26.721 --> 12:28.431
fangirl journey began for my sister.

199
12:28.961 --> 12:30.761
Does she have something to say?

200
12:30.861 --> 12:32.661
What's gotten into her since yesterday?

201
12:32.661 --> 12:33.901
(Episode 2: The Gap)

202
12:36.331 --> 12:38.371
- Tae Gu. Hey. - Hey.

203
12:38.671 --> 12:40.271
- Hey. - Are you okay?

204
12:45.941 --> 12:46.981
Seriously.

205
12:49.681 --> 12:51.381
Hey, Go Eun Young!

206
12:54.181 --> 12:55.451
Ji Young.

207
12:56.421 --> 12:58.491
What? What is it?

208
12:58.721 --> 13:02.961
Why? What happened? Wait a second.

209
13:05.361 --> 13:06.801
What?

210
13:08.001 --> 13:09.201
A pigeon?

211
13:09.601 --> 13:12.641
He said it would be nice to have a real pigeon for the evaluation.

212
13:14.071 --> 13:18.581
So you actually caught one for him? He was obviously just saying that.

213
13:20.641 --> 13:21.751
Really?

214
13:22.511 --> 13:24.821
Your reaction is even more shocking to me.

215
13:25.921 --> 13:28.591
You didn't cause any other trouble, did you?

216
13:30.221 --> 13:31.221
A nosebleed.

217
13:31.521 --> 13:32.661
What?

218
13:32.961 --> 13:35.791
I got caught while running away, and my head flew forward,

219
13:36.531 --> 13:37.831
so I went like this,

220
13:38.361 --> 13:39.531
and he went like this,

221
13:40.331 --> 13:41.401
and then...

222
13:42.971 --> 13:45.901
Gosh, you hardheaded idiot.

223
13:47.141 --> 13:49.141
No way. I can't cover for this.

224
13:50.771 --> 13:52.311
Just come clean and own it.

225
13:52.381 --> 13:54.611
Tell them you're their fan and that you like them.

226
13:54.681 --> 13:55.681
No.

227
13:56.581 --> 14:00.281
I like watching them from afar like this.

228
14:01.891 --> 14:03.091
Are you a pervert?

229
14:06.991 --> 14:08.131
I don't know.

230
14:08.961 --> 14:10.131
I'm going to sleep.

231
14:10.531 --> 14:12.601
Wait, sit down for a second.

232
14:14.061 --> 14:15.201
Let me ask you one thing.

233
14:15.901 --> 14:19.171
Why them? I don't get you at all,

234
14:19.241 --> 14:20.471
but this makes the least sense to me.

235
14:20.871 --> 14:23.641
Out of all the celebrities, why does it have to be them?

236
14:26.611 --> 14:27.781
It feels warm.

237
14:30.951 --> 14:32.851
When I watch the three of them,

238
14:35.191 --> 14:39.461
it feels like my heart is warming up.

239
14:42.331 --> 14:43.461
I like that.

240
14:47.401 --> 14:48.571
Yes, you're definitely a pervert.

241
14:55.611 --> 14:56.841
You hardheaded idiot.

242
15:01.311 --> 15:03.751
Hey, stop touching it. You'll make it worse.

243
15:03.781 --> 15:04.781
Let me see.

244
15:04.781 --> 15:06.681
I mean, how hard did you get headbutted...

245
15:06.751 --> 15:08.051
to end up with blood pouring from both nostrils?

246
15:08.121 --> 15:10.021
It's only this bad because I have quick reflexes.

247
15:10.221 --> 15:11.621
That was not a human skull.

248
15:11.861 --> 15:13.291
Of all days, on evaluation day.

249
15:14.191 --> 15:17.791
Hey, could those drinks from before have been sent by that woman too?

250
15:22.231 --> 15:23.331
Hey, you're right.

251
15:23.501 --> 15:26.371
Man, I think we're being targeted by the neighbourhood lunatic.

252
15:27.671 --> 15:29.711
If we at least knew what she looked like, we could report her.

253
15:29.941 --> 15:32.041
Why would we report her?

254
15:32.181 --> 15:33.711
I'll track her down and destroy her myself.

255
15:35.511 --> 15:38.651
Just wait till I catch you, black scarf. Darn it.

256
15:43.521 --> 15:45.221
- Hello, sir. - Hi.

257
15:45.321 --> 15:47.321
(Segment review)

258
15:47.621 --> 15:49.591
You guys are really putting your lives on the line.

259
15:50.791 --> 15:53.931
Why is everyone working so hard?

260
15:55.931 --> 15:58.101
Do well. I'll be expecting a lot.

261
15:58.701 --> 16:01.611
Sure. But you know what?

262
16:06.011 --> 16:07.741
I'm not expecting anything from you.

263
16:13.051 --> 16:16.251
- Tae Gu. - Chan Sung's team, you're up first.

264
16:16.691 --> 16:17.691
Yes, ma'am.

265
16:21.121 --> 16:23.331
- Let's go. - Give me a break.

266
16:23.861 --> 16:25.901
- Hello. - Hey.

267
16:26.161 --> 16:28.161
Hey, let's run through it one more time.

268
16:31.771 --> 16:33.201
Hang in there!

269
16:34.341 --> 16:36.371
(Gag Jirak)

270
16:38.481 --> 16:39.641
(QBN Entertainment)

271
16:39.641 --> 16:44.551
- Hang in there! - Hang in there!

272
17:01.401 --> 17:04.231
- Great job. Great job, sir. - Thank you.

273
17:21.081 --> 17:25.761
We're being filmed!

274
17:28.791 --> 17:30.191
Hey, good job, everyone.

275
17:30.631 --> 17:31.761
We made it.

276
17:34.031 --> 17:36.031
I wonder if their segment check went well.

277
17:36.401 --> 17:38.371
Curious again, are you?

278
17:39.341 --> 17:40.941
I am scared, but I am curious.

279
17:42.071 --> 17:43.511
Curious, yet terrified.

280
17:44.911 --> 17:48.751
That is why you should just open it. You are so frustrating.

281
17:49.981 --> 17:51.251
Do whatever you want.

282
17:52.051 --> 17:54.351
Let us go eat out before heading home.

283
17:54.451 --> 17:55.451
What do you say?

284
17:55.521 --> 17:57.621
How about there? That looks good. Let us go.

285
17:58.291 --> 17:59.861
Shall we get skewers? Come on.

286
18:00.091 --> 18:01.521
Let's go!

287
18:01.521 --> 18:03.461
Looking here

288
18:05.661 --> 18:07.131
And looking there

289
18:08.371 --> 18:10.031
All right.

290
18:10.731 --> 18:13.141
The vibe in here is nice. It looks different from the outside.

291
18:13.401 --> 18:14.471
How many in your party?

292
18:17.611 --> 18:20.381
- Hey. - Cafe lady.

293
18:22.611 --> 18:24.051
Hey, let us go somewhere else.

294
18:25.011 --> 18:26.651
No.

295
18:27.321 --> 18:30.091
Hello. You are Asura, right?

296
18:31.051 --> 18:32.821
I am the cafe lady's little sister.

297
18:32.891 --> 18:34.691
I have heard so much about you from her.

298
18:35.461 --> 18:39.261
- About us? - Yes. Just that comedians...

299
18:39.331 --> 18:40.961
were regulars at her cafe, that kind of thing.

300
18:41.531 --> 18:43.431
These seats are really nice, though.

301
18:44.001 --> 18:45.371
Since we ran into each other,

302
18:45.941 --> 18:47.501
do you mind if we join you?

303
18:49.811 --> 18:50.811
Eun Young!

304
18:51.141 --> 18:52.781
Please have a seat. Sit down.

305
18:53.081 --> 18:54.211
Is something wrong with him?

306
18:55.181 --> 18:57.081
- The owner here... - Please sit.

307
18:57.151 --> 18:58.151
Where is the owner?

308
18:58.211 --> 18:59.621
- The owner. - The owner over there.

309
18:59.681 --> 19:03.021
I was actually a piano major. I was such an attention seeker,

310
19:03.091 --> 19:04.691
and wearing a gown under the spotlight...

311
19:04.821 --> 19:06.961
while playing the piano just looked so cool.

312
19:07.161 --> 19:09.291
Well, I got bored and quit eventually, though.

313
19:09.391 --> 19:11.631
Anyway, I took a leave from school...

314
19:11.761 --> 19:12.861
and worked all sorts of part-time jobs.

315
19:12.931 --> 19:16.031
Recently, I worked at a surf house in Yangyang,

316
19:16.271 --> 19:18.201
but I guess I quit that because Toma told me to.

317
19:18.271 --> 19:20.301
He was a Romanian guy travelling in Korea,

318
19:20.371 --> 19:21.741
and we dated for a bit.

319
19:21.871 --> 19:23.271
He was way too clingy, though.

320
19:23.341 --> 19:24.971
He told me, "You like too many things other than me."

321
19:25.041 --> 19:27.241
That is what he said. He had a point, actually.

322
19:27.311 --> 19:28.511
So I dumped him right away.

323
19:29.951 --> 19:31.451
Wait, what was the first question again?

324
19:31.511 --> 19:33.481
- Nobody asked a question. - Right.

325
19:34.251 --> 19:35.691
Why I live as a freeter.

326
19:37.551 --> 19:41.591
My tattoo, que sera, sera. That is my motto.

327
19:41.891 --> 19:44.131
Going wherever destiny takes me.

328
19:44.191 --> 19:45.401
If you do that, you will eventually end up somewhere,

329
19:45.461 --> 19:47.761
- will you not? - Destiny.

330
19:47.831 --> 19:51.941
Destiny sounds so cool, doesn't it? Wait, but she...

331
19:52.001 --> 19:53.441
must've been really hungry.

332
19:53.771 --> 19:56.341
Could she be uncomfortable because of us?

333
19:56.411 --> 19:58.911
- That could be it. - Uncomfortable?

334
19:58.981 --> 20:00.611
If anything, we are grateful.

335
20:01.011 --> 20:03.081
So, what were you talking about before we got here?

336
20:03.151 --> 20:04.611
It sounded like good news.

337
20:06.281 --> 20:07.821
Well, after such a long time,

338
20:07.981 --> 20:11.351
- we finally got to tape a show... - Really?

339
20:11.491 --> 20:12.761
Congratulations!

340
20:13.121 --> 20:15.761
Well, taping shows is just part of being a comedian.

341
20:15.891 --> 20:17.791
Man, you never know where life will take you, right?

342
20:18.261 --> 20:20.501
Oh, I should tell you about this.

343
20:20.631 --> 20:22.331
You said you two live in this neighbourhood, right?

344
20:22.901 --> 20:25.031
- Yes. - She might be watching.

345
20:25.131 --> 20:26.171
Lean in a bit.

346
20:27.241 --> 20:29.011
Around here,

347
20:29.941 --> 20:31.271
there is a crazy woman.

348
20:31.811 --> 20:35.781
She hung spoiled drinks on our doorknob.

349
20:38.481 --> 20:41.221
And she stuffed live pigeons into a burlap sack...

350
20:41.281 --> 20:42.291
and left them right at our front door.

351
20:42.351 --> 20:45.261
And when he went after her... Look right here.

352
20:45.321 --> 20:47.521
She completely broke his nose like this.

353
20:47.661 --> 20:49.591
She headbutted him and broke it just like that.

354
20:50.061 --> 20:52.231
It hurts, stop touching it.

355
20:52.661 --> 20:54.301
She sounds completely crazy.

356
20:56.471 --> 20:58.171
You really need to be careful.

357
20:58.871 --> 21:00.401
You too, ma'am. Be careful.

358
21:01.101 --> 21:04.371
I said I was sorry. You didn't get caught.

359
21:04.441 --> 21:06.711
- You are fine. - Seriously!

360
21:09.651 --> 21:12.081
He called me a crazy woman.

361
21:12.151 --> 21:14.021
- A crazy woman... - But still,

362
21:14.081 --> 21:16.591
to be honest, since they were washed-up comedians,

363
21:16.651 --> 21:19.591
I didn't expect anything at all, but they are kind of fun.

364
21:20.361 --> 21:21.821
Who is your favourite?

365
21:23.391 --> 21:24.391
What?

366
21:24.461 --> 21:26.001
Which of the three do you like best?

367
21:26.061 --> 21:27.531
I don't have a favourite.

368
21:27.601 --> 21:30.301
Of course you do. Being a fan is all about attraction.

369
21:30.371 --> 21:31.531
Mine is Jun Seo.

370
21:32.401 --> 21:36.141
I am always drawn to those straight-laced types.

371
21:36.341 --> 21:38.011
It makes me want to unravel him.

372
21:38.581 --> 21:39.811
Stop it.

373
21:41.441 --> 21:43.051
I really just like them...

374
21:43.481 --> 21:45.951
purely as a fan, okay?

375
21:45.981 --> 21:48.481
Sure. Whatever you say.

376
21:51.321 --> 21:54.261
They must be so thrilled they won't even sleep tonight.

377
22:00.831 --> 22:02.101
Probably.

378
22:02.701 --> 22:04.671
They waited so long for this.

379
22:06.241 --> 22:08.671
I have definitely seen her somewhere.

380
22:09.241 --> 22:10.511
Where was it?

381
22:14.811 --> 22:16.111
Hello?

382
22:16.651 --> 22:19.521
- Na Yeon. - Oh, darn.

383
22:19.651 --> 22:20.851
Don't freak out.

384
22:21.481 --> 22:23.151
Our sketch got approved.

385
22:24.551 --> 22:26.521
We are taping tomorrow.

386
22:27.161 --> 22:30.031
You will come watch, right? We should throw a celebration party.

387
22:30.491 --> 22:31.891
Just the two of us, without them.

388
22:32.431 --> 22:33.661
- Hey. - I am not going anyway.

389
22:33.731 --> 22:35.801
- Even if you beg me, darn it. - Remember...

390
22:35.871 --> 22:38.871
that place you wanted to go, the Japanese restaurant?

391
22:38.971 --> 22:42.041
Really? Sounds great. Of course it is on me.

392
22:42.911 --> 22:46.081
- No, I am paying for it. - What a shallow jerk.

393
22:46.481 --> 22:49.481
He just wants to show off. It has been a while.

394
22:50.081 --> 22:52.021
Are you not inviting your family?

395
22:52.321 --> 22:53.921
It is hard for Hyun Gu to get around,

396
22:54.381 --> 22:56.621
and Dad could not care less.

397
22:56.691 --> 22:59.321
- Still, you never know. - Forget it.

398
23:02.761 --> 23:04.631
Hey, Hyun Gu. What are you doing?

399
23:04.831 --> 23:06.861
- Talking to you, obviously. - What about Dad?

400
23:06.931 --> 23:10.201
- He is right next to me. Why? - It is nothing, but...

401
23:12.401 --> 23:14.341
about that car repair booked for tomorrow,

402
23:15.041 --> 23:16.411
I think we will have to push it back a day.

403
23:16.471 --> 23:17.811
Why, again?

404
23:17.911 --> 23:19.311
A shoot was scheduled out of nowhere.

405
23:19.411 --> 23:20.411
A sh...

406
23:21.041 --> 23:22.951
- A shoot? - Yes.

407
23:23.111 --> 23:24.681
Seriously?

408
23:25.421 --> 23:26.421
So?

409
23:27.551 --> 23:29.121
The new producer apparently,

410
23:29.191 --> 23:31.921
has always loved my comedy or something like that.

411
23:32.921 --> 23:36.031
- He wanted to tape right away. - See? What did I tell you?

412
23:36.091 --> 23:39.101
I told you this year would be your year, didn't I?

413
23:39.101 --> 23:41.731
I did all the work. Why are you taking all the credit?

414
23:43.071 --> 23:44.071
Hey.

415
23:44.231 --> 23:47.441
- So anyway, I was wondering... - What time is it?

416
23:47.741 --> 23:50.011
I will come watch. What time should I be there?

417
23:50.271 --> 23:53.341
What? Never mind.

418
23:53.681 --> 23:54.681
It is no big deal.

419
23:54.741 --> 23:56.151
Do not trouble yourself coming all this way.

420
23:56.211 --> 23:59.721
It is no trouble at all. I will bring Dad along too.

421
23:59.751 --> 24:02.721
Come on! Forget it.

422
24:03.321 --> 24:05.091
It is not worth bothering Dad over.

423
24:06.961 --> 24:07.961
Don't you have appointments tomorrow?

424
24:08.021 --> 24:09.461
Even if we do, we will clear them, you punk.

425
24:09.761 --> 24:10.891
All right, hang up.

426
24:11.591 --> 24:12.601
Yes.

427
24:14.731 --> 24:15.731
Dad.

428
24:17.231 --> 24:18.231
Did you hear that?

429
24:18.771 --> 24:20.501
Tae Gu is filming tomorrow.

430
24:23.941 --> 24:25.441
He wants us there so badly,

431
24:25.511 --> 24:28.141
but he was too shy to say it, so he kept beating around the bush.

432
24:30.051 --> 24:32.481
The sketch they put together this time must be really good.

433
24:32.581 --> 24:34.851
He said everyone around them is raving about it.

434
24:37.821 --> 24:40.661
- You still believe that punk? - Come on.

435
24:40.821 --> 24:43.261
If an older brother does not believe in his little brother,

436
24:43.791 --> 24:46.761
who will? Just think about it.

437
24:46.831 --> 24:49.571
When Mom passed away, and when I had my accident...

438
24:49.631 --> 24:51.001
If it were not for Tae Gu, where would we...

439
24:51.431 --> 24:52.441
He might fool around, but...

440
24:52.501 --> 24:55.141
- It is late. Let us sleep. - Yes, sir.

441
24:56.071 --> 24:57.771
We're supposed to go to the taping tomorrow,

442
24:57.841 --> 24:58.941
so you should come too.

443
24:59.611 --> 25:00.641
I have an appointment.

444
25:01.141 --> 25:03.111
You can reschedule it.

445
25:10.421 --> 25:11.921
Go to sleep, guys.

446
25:11.991 --> 25:14.761
- Don't you have a taping tomorrow? - Are we really taping tomorrow?

447
25:14.961 --> 25:17.891
- Why doesn't it feel real? - Hey, this won't do.

448
25:17.991 --> 25:19.231
Let's hit each other...

449
25:19.301 --> 25:20.361
and knock each other out.

450
25:20.431 --> 25:21.431
Hey, hit him.

451
25:23.271 --> 25:24.431
Honestly,

452
25:24.931 --> 25:27.071
I thought we would never even get on stage...

453
25:27.141 --> 25:28.301
before it ended.

454
25:29.571 --> 25:31.241
So this feels like a dream right now.

455
25:31.871 --> 25:34.411
I'm going to treat this like my last chance,

456
25:34.481 --> 25:37.781
and I'll give it my all. And then I'll definitely succeed,

457
25:38.051 --> 25:39.281
so I can pay back Na Yeon...

458
25:39.621 --> 25:42.251
and my parents who sold soup in the market...

459
25:42.321 --> 25:45.421
for those ten long years.

460
25:48.391 --> 25:50.131
That's why you need to go to sleep.

461
26:04.371 --> 26:06.281
I told you to go to bed early, you jerk.

462
26:06.341 --> 26:07.481
Hey, hurry up!

463
26:07.541 --> 26:09.251
- Flush properly if you take a dump. - I didn't notice.

464
26:09.451 --> 26:10.451
Get in, quickly.

465
26:11.451 --> 26:12.451
Get in already.

466
26:13.551 --> 26:15.221
Do your best.

467
26:16.421 --> 26:17.651
You've got this.

468
26:19.991 --> 26:22.531
(The Perfect Cleaning Experts: Clean Team)

469
26:28.361 --> 26:29.801
They said they're doing the opening act.

470
26:30.471 --> 26:31.671
Really?

471
26:31.731 --> 26:32.841
(New, Energetic Family)

472
26:35.971 --> 26:38.441
It would've been nice if Father had come too.

473
26:39.181 --> 26:40.211
I know.

474
26:44.011 --> 26:45.081
You're here already?

475
26:46.281 --> 26:47.321
Dad.

476
26:49.351 --> 26:50.451
Give me your ticket.

477
26:50.791 --> 26:51.791
Why?

478
26:52.961 --> 26:54.261
You're here, Dad.

479
26:58.731 --> 27:00.031
Come this way.

480
27:01.731 --> 27:04.701
The number one live comedy show in Korea.

481
27:04.871 --> 27:09.111
Welcome to Gag Jirak, everyone.

482
27:12.411 --> 27:16.351
- Are you ready to laugh, everyone? - Yes.

483
27:16.411 --> 27:18.981
If you're ready, make some noise.

484
27:22.851 --> 27:25.351
- Well, today... - Hey, Nam Il.

485
27:25.421 --> 27:27.561
Come here. Look.

486
27:28.061 --> 27:29.591
Over there, isn't that Na Yeon?

487
27:30.091 --> 27:31.531
Yes, it is.

488
27:32.091 --> 27:33.931
Hey, Tae Gu.

489
27:34.101 --> 27:37.631
- Come here. - We'll kick things off with a gift!

490
27:37.801 --> 27:38.801
Look over there.

491
27:39.371 --> 27:40.371
Look.

492
27:41.171 --> 27:43.271
Has anyone here never,

493
27:43.341 --> 27:46.141
- not even once, won a giveaway... - Dad.

494
27:46.381 --> 27:48.681
at an event like this?

495
27:49.651 --> 27:52.181
All right, for the first sketch, everyone has their mics on, right?

496
27:53.121 --> 27:54.151
Okay.

497
27:54.981 --> 27:57.351
Yes, understood. Yes, just a moment.

498
27:57.421 --> 27:58.921
Producer, you have a phone call.

499
27:59.161 --> 28:00.961
- Right now? - Yes.

500
28:01.461 --> 28:06.401
To kick off Gag Jirak with a bang, here is our first sketch.

501
28:06.931 --> 28:09.201
It is an ambitious new segment...

502
28:09.271 --> 28:12.031
being presented to you for the very first time.

503
28:12.301 --> 28:13.501
They are coming out now.

504
28:13.571 --> 28:15.241
(Kim Nam Il is the best.)

505
28:17.311 --> 28:19.381
Let us go, Asura.

506
28:19.541 --> 28:20.611
- Balbalta. - Balbalta.

507
28:23.481 --> 28:24.881
Stop.

508
28:25.451 --> 28:26.981
I am really sorry. Hold on a second.

509
28:27.221 --> 28:28.551
- What is it? - Just a second.

510
28:29.891 --> 28:31.521
- What is going on? - Just a second.

511
28:36.531 --> 28:38.461
- Did you check the volume? - Yes.

512
28:38.531 --> 28:41.631
- I do not think you did. - I did. Break a leg.

513
28:47.501 --> 28:49.571
- I will give you the signal. - Sorry.

514
28:50.941 --> 28:51.941
Please welcome...

515
28:53.311 --> 28:55.011
- Team... - Pick it up.

516
28:55.881 --> 28:57.051
- Hwang-sman. - Shall we go?

517
28:57.111 --> 28:58.111
Let us go.

518
29:03.721 --> 29:05.321
(Kim Nam Il is the best.)

519
29:05.621 --> 29:07.161
Wait, weren't they supposed to go first?

520
29:07.361 --> 29:08.361
Yes, they were.

521
29:08.421 --> 29:10.391
Was this not originally our boys' slot?

522
29:10.531 --> 29:11.991
First up.

523
29:13.761 --> 29:16.001
- Hwang Chan Sung. - Hold on just a bit longer.

524
29:16.071 --> 29:20.501
- Hwang Chan Sung. - Hwang Chan Sung.

525
29:21.241 --> 29:23.511
- Who is it? - Hwang Chan Sung.

526
29:26.181 --> 29:29.251
- Hey, Nam Il. - Hwang Chan Sung.

527
29:29.311 --> 29:32.281
- Hwang Chan Sung. - Hwang Chan Sung.

528
29:32.751 --> 29:36.451
All right, then let us begin recording the first sketch.

529
29:36.591 --> 29:37.591
Here we go.

530
29:47.801 --> 29:48.931
Does this make any sense?

531
29:49.401 --> 29:51.771
You swapped the sketch without the producer's approval?

532
29:51.831 --> 29:55.571
- Right before taping? - I kept telling you.

533
29:55.641 --> 29:57.341
Cut those guys and put in Hwang Chan Sung.

534
29:57.911 --> 30:01.211
Yet you insisted, right? You turned off your phone to stall...

535
30:01.511 --> 30:02.951
just so you could do whatever you wanted.

536
30:03.011 --> 30:04.011
What choice did I have?

537
30:04.711 --> 30:07.921
- I had to arrange it myself. - Hwang Chan...

538
30:08.381 --> 30:09.951
Hwang Chan Sung's stuff is predictable.

539
30:10.091 --> 30:11.991
Those guys are so much fresher.

540
30:14.021 --> 30:15.931
This is reality, okay?

541
30:19.061 --> 30:21.401
I told you to make a new sketch...

542
30:21.461 --> 30:23.601
to bury that producer replacement controversy,

543
30:24.101 --> 30:26.541
and you brought in total nobodies.

544
30:27.441 --> 30:28.801
So that is what it comes down to? Name value?

545
30:29.241 --> 30:31.171
Is that really a good enough excuse...

546
30:31.241 --> 30:32.811
to cut kids who passed the evaluation fair and square?

547
30:33.511 --> 30:36.351
Hey, what better reason is there?

548
30:36.811 --> 30:38.851
Besides, we cannot afford to lose Hwang Chan Sung.

549
30:39.181 --> 30:41.521
It is already nerve-racking enough that TVS is launching...

550
30:41.581 --> 30:42.621
a live audience comedy show.

551
30:43.451 --> 30:45.321
What if Hwang Chan Sung gets offended and jumps ship?

552
30:45.391 --> 30:47.191
All the more reason to raise these kids.

553
30:47.261 --> 30:49.331
That way, guys like Hwang Chan Sung cannot push us around.

554
30:49.391 --> 30:51.491
Is this a daycare? Why are you trying to raise them?

555
30:54.231 --> 30:55.301
Stop talking nonsense,

556
30:55.361 --> 30:57.971
call Hwang Chan Sung in tomorrow, and keep him happy.

557
30:58.401 --> 31:01.041
Do not stir up trouble. Just keep things running.

558
31:01.371 --> 31:02.371
That is your job.

559
31:11.311 --> 31:13.821
It is because of our name recognition, right?

560
31:16.391 --> 31:17.651
It will be tough next week too, right?

561
31:20.061 --> 31:21.161
Oh, how petty.

562
31:21.691 --> 31:22.891
The pettiest thing in the world...

563
31:22.991 --> 31:24.061
is giving something and taking it back.

564
31:25.231 --> 31:26.261
I am sorry.

565
31:27.301 --> 31:29.671
Our internal circumstances are...

566
31:29.731 --> 31:31.901
I am sure the production crew had their reasons.

567
31:33.301 --> 31:34.301
Still,

568
31:36.311 --> 31:37.471
to understand all that,

569
31:39.211 --> 31:41.341
today's stage was...

570
31:42.851 --> 31:43.951
something we were desperate for.

571
31:54.461 --> 31:55.721
Thank you for the opportunity.

572
31:56.431 --> 31:57.761
See you at the new segment review.

573
32:04.431 --> 32:05.431
So,

574
32:05.501 --> 32:07.541
we are going to put together a new segment and try again.

575
32:08.601 --> 32:10.311
It is dirty and petty, but what choice do we have?

576
32:10.911 --> 32:12.411
We are the desperate ones, so we have to suck it up.

577
32:12.841 --> 32:14.081
Looking at it objectively,

578
32:14.841 --> 32:16.081
we were just mediocre.

579
32:16.581 --> 32:18.181
If we were really funny, they would have taped it.

580
32:18.511 --> 32:19.521
Right?

581
32:35.661 --> 32:38.871
(Reserved by Kim Nam Il for 2, May 8, 5:30pm)

582
33:00.061 --> 33:01.061
This is so good.

583
33:01.691 --> 33:02.691
Try this.

584
33:08.061 --> 33:09.131
It is amazing.

585
33:13.441 --> 33:15.201
- Nam Il. - Na Yeon.

586
33:16.011 --> 33:17.041
Try the salmon.

587
33:17.741 --> 33:19.411
Otherwise, I might eat it all.

588
33:21.181 --> 33:24.451
- About yesterday... - Na Yeon.

589
33:28.681 --> 33:30.291
I am fine.

590
33:35.821 --> 33:38.661
What should we have next?

591
33:41.201 --> 33:42.701
Let us get the yellowtail.

592
33:43.071 --> 33:44.801
- Check, please. - Sure.

593
33:47.041 --> 33:49.641
Your party has already paid.

594
33:51.041 --> 33:54.141
- Course A for two... - Yes, it has been paid.

595
34:04.421 --> 34:06.521
That cafe looks nice. Let us go there.

596
34:08.661 --> 34:09.661
How much was it?

597
34:12.661 --> 34:14.161
Forget it.

598
34:14.561 --> 34:15.901
You buy the coffee.

599
34:17.071 --> 34:18.071
How much was it?

600
34:29.681 --> 34:31.051
It's 140 dollars per person.

601
34:37.791 --> 34:39.821
I will wire you the rest.

602
34:41.921 --> 34:42.931
Let's go.

603
34:58.141 --> 34:59.141
Aren't you coming?

604
35:02.041 --> 35:04.511
- Shall we talk at the cafe? - Let go.

605
35:10.551 --> 35:13.461
If you were going to be like this, you should have cancelled.

606
35:15.161 --> 35:16.631
Why did we even meet today?

607
35:19.031 --> 35:21.661
- I am sorry. - Have I ever once nagged you...

608
35:21.801 --> 35:22.871
about not being on air?

609
35:25.171 --> 35:28.471
- No. - I came out today to comfort you.

610
35:29.571 --> 35:30.941
I stayed up all night...

611
35:31.871 --> 35:33.311
thinking about what to say.

612
35:35.241 --> 35:36.911
Yet, you will not even let me speak.

613
35:38.111 --> 35:40.921
Who cares who pays for this meal? Why does that matter so much?

614
35:42.121 --> 35:43.191
Are you that angry?

615
36:03.171 --> 36:04.171
Yes.

616
36:06.741 --> 36:07.741
I am angry.

617
36:10.111 --> 36:11.551
I am so mad.

618
36:17.021 --> 36:19.991
Sure, a guy might look pathetic in front of his girlfriend.

619
36:21.221 --> 36:22.861
He can seek comfort when times are tough.

620
36:22.931 --> 36:24.631
If he has no money, she can buy him a meal.

621
36:24.691 --> 36:26.091
But Na Yeon,

622
36:27.601 --> 36:28.961
it has been ten years.

623
36:30.371 --> 36:33.371
After whining and mooching for ten years,

624
36:37.311 --> 36:40.511
I just wanted to look cool for once,

625
36:41.511 --> 36:43.511
and I could not even do that right.

626
36:45.781 --> 36:47.851
It makes me so angry and humiliated.

627
36:49.321 --> 36:51.621
I am so mad at myself for being a loser.

628
36:51.691 --> 36:52.691
Are you an idiot?

629
36:55.121 --> 36:56.491
What do you mean, a loser?

630
36:58.131 --> 36:59.701
Why would you think that?

631
37:05.131 --> 37:07.071
Have you really never thought of me that way?

632
37:11.911 --> 37:12.911
What?

633
37:52.551 --> 37:53.781
It is a promotion gift.

634
37:56.991 --> 37:57.991
Congratulations.

635
38:07.901 --> 38:10.331
I wanted to give it to you at the cafe. I am sorry.

636
38:11.131 --> 38:12.731
- Nam Il. - Na Yeon.

637
38:14.671 --> 38:16.211
I was okay being the boyfriend...

638
38:17.771 --> 38:20.381
who only receives comfort. But...

639
38:24.751 --> 38:26.351
A man who cannot even celebrate you...

640
38:42.831 --> 38:44.971
I am sorry, Na Yeon. I cannot walk you home today.

641
38:46.231 --> 38:47.501
Get home safe, okay?

642
38:48.001 --> 38:49.041
I will call you.

643
38:49.541 --> 38:50.571
I love you.

644
39:03.491 --> 39:06.521
(Eunhye Auto Repair Shop)

645
39:08.091 --> 39:09.191
Seriously.

646
39:09.991 --> 39:11.031
Darn...

647
39:11.661 --> 39:14.101
They are total scumbags, all of them.

648
39:15.401 --> 39:16.831
Hey, what year is this?

649
39:17.131 --> 39:18.771
Pulling a power trip like that?

650
39:18.971 --> 39:20.141
Do not let that get you down.

651
39:20.371 --> 39:22.041
I will kill you if you do, seriously.

652
39:22.801 --> 39:24.211
Are you comforting me or threatening me?

653
39:24.471 --> 39:25.711
Stop talking and eat. You are spitting.

654
39:25.771 --> 39:27.941
That Hwang Chan Sung guy is not even funny.

655
39:28.011 --> 39:29.511
He looks like a dried-up shrimp, really.

656
39:29.581 --> 39:30.581
I said you are spitting!

657
39:30.651 --> 39:32.711
- Really. - You.

658
39:38.651 --> 39:39.861
Give it up already.

659
39:46.291 --> 39:47.601
You should know by now.

660
39:50.131 --> 39:51.501
When it is not working, it is not working.

661
40:00.611 --> 40:01.611
No.

662
40:02.481 --> 40:03.751
I am just getting started.

663
40:03.951 --> 40:05.851
I am going to do comedy until the day I die.

664
40:06.651 --> 40:07.721
Even when I am in a coffin,

665
40:07.821 --> 40:09.321
I will be posing like this.

666
40:10.191 --> 40:11.721
You crazy punk. Stop it.

667
40:13.391 --> 40:14.391
What?

668
40:23.171 --> 40:25.131
If I was going to quit like this, I would not have started.

669
40:28.441 --> 40:29.941
So you should be the one to give up, Dad.

670
40:32.471 --> 40:33.481
You know how I am.

671
40:34.011 --> 40:35.041
I am stubborn.

672
40:46.591 --> 40:47.821
You selfish brat.

673
40:54.061 --> 40:55.161
Dad.

674
40:56.471 --> 40:57.501
Leave him, Hyun Gu.

675
40:58.401 --> 41:00.041
I am a selfish brat, so what?

676
41:15.121 --> 41:16.181
Hey, where is Nam Il?

677
41:16.451 --> 41:17.951
Did you not tell him we had a meeting for the gig?

678
41:18.091 --> 41:19.991
Well, I told him this morning...

679
41:21.061 --> 41:22.061
Yes, sir.

680
41:23.331 --> 41:24.591
Look who is here.

681
41:28.501 --> 41:29.831
Hey, did you drink?

682
41:30.501 --> 41:32.031
I told you we have a meeting.

683
41:33.741 --> 41:34.741
I am sorry.

684
41:35.901 --> 41:37.641
I am sorry. I deserve to die.

685
41:37.711 --> 41:40.141
- I totally forgot. - Great job, Kim Nam Il.

686
41:40.681 --> 41:43.251
Hey, even if it is just us, you need to separate work and life.

687
41:49.951 --> 41:50.991
What is with you?

688
41:51.621 --> 41:52.921
Hey.

689
41:53.491 --> 41:54.521
Hey.

690
41:57.031 --> 42:00.061
What professional life do we even have?

691
42:01.761 --> 42:04.401
Does bickering among ourselves count as work?

692
42:05.201 --> 42:06.201
Darn it.

693
42:08.771 --> 42:11.741
It is just a bunch of pathetic losers killing time.

694
42:13.411 --> 42:15.341
- What? - Hey, Nam Il,

695
42:15.411 --> 42:16.981
did something bad happen?

696
42:17.851 --> 42:19.651
Something bad happens every day.

697
42:21.721 --> 42:22.721
Hey.

698
42:24.621 --> 42:25.621
Hey, but...

699
42:30.031 --> 42:31.731
How long are we going to do this?

700
42:35.231 --> 42:36.461
We made a promise.

701
42:38.231 --> 42:39.231
Ten years.

702
42:40.201 --> 42:41.841
I think ten years are up.

703
42:48.381 --> 42:49.541
Why look so surprised, you punks?

704
42:49.611 --> 42:51.951
Deep down, you were both thinking it too.

705
42:52.011 --> 42:54.421
Darn it. I will...

706
42:59.391 --> 43:00.461
I will just...

707
43:02.491 --> 43:03.691
make the call for us.

708
43:09.161 --> 43:10.231
Let us quit.

709
43:12.531 --> 43:13.671
Asura is over.

710
43:19.171 --> 43:20.181
Hey.

711
43:20.911 --> 43:24.081
He is drunk, right? Hey, I think he is drunk.

712
43:24.081 --> 43:26.181
Let us talk in the morning. He is drunk.

713
43:26.251 --> 43:28.151
- Tae Gu. - Hey, Kim Nam Il.

714
43:28.821 --> 43:31.121
- What did you just say? - What?

715
43:31.121 --> 43:33.021
I do not care how drunk you are!

716
43:33.721 --> 43:34.991
There are some lines you do not cross.

717
43:35.061 --> 43:36.391
It is because I am sick of it!

718
43:40.261 --> 43:41.261
Hey.

719
43:41.831 --> 43:44.031
I am sick of this moldy place,

720
43:44.831 --> 43:47.341
and sweating through my underwear...

721
43:47.641 --> 43:50.641
down in that parking garage until I am sticky every single day.

722
43:53.281 --> 43:54.281
Darn it.

723
43:54.441 --> 43:56.241
I am sick of our sketches getting rejected.

724
43:56.541 --> 43:59.781
Every time they reject us, I am sick of putting on a brave face...

725
43:59.981 --> 44:01.721
and pretending to cheer each other up.

726
44:03.351 --> 44:04.451
I am sick of all of it.

727
44:06.721 --> 44:08.091
Hey, let us be real here.

728
44:08.691 --> 44:10.731
In the last few years,

729
44:11.261 --> 44:13.361
has anyone treated you like real human beings?

730
44:17.301 --> 44:18.501
Look at Jun Seo.

731
44:20.271 --> 44:21.471
Darn it.

732
44:22.241 --> 44:23.271
His family...

733
44:23.741 --> 44:25.341
gave up on him ages ago.

734
44:27.041 --> 44:29.611
And you are exhausted from your dad hounding you.

735
44:33.581 --> 44:34.721
Hey, but...

736
44:36.951 --> 44:39.521
Darn it, those people are not the bad guys.

737
44:40.961 --> 44:42.021
We...

738
44:42.891 --> 44:44.461
made them that way.

739
44:47.431 --> 44:49.101
- Nam Il. - Na Yeon...

740
44:50.631 --> 44:52.831
Someone so kind and honest...

741
44:56.171 --> 44:57.971
is turning into a liar because of me.

742
45:00.711 --> 45:01.711
Do you have any idea...

743
45:01.781 --> 45:03.111
what it feels like watching that happen?

744
45:05.211 --> 45:07.551
All right. We got your point.

745
45:07.551 --> 45:08.721
Are you the only one having a hard time?

746
45:10.291 --> 45:11.621
It is hard on me too!

747
45:14.121 --> 45:16.521
I am sucking it up every single day. So why do you always act like...

748
45:16.591 --> 45:19.091
Then do not suck it up! Hey, do not hold it in!

749
45:19.431 --> 45:21.661
Let us stop holding it in. Stop it, please.

750
45:24.931 --> 45:26.171
Seriously, guys.

751
45:26.901 --> 45:30.311
If we just quit right now, do you think there is anyone...

752
45:31.171 --> 45:32.341
who would actually try to stop us?

753
45:33.141 --> 45:34.141
No one.

754
45:37.981 --> 45:40.281
We are just a bunch of nobodies who got together,

755
45:40.981 --> 45:42.521
and we are just desperately flailing around.

756
46:22.091 --> 46:23.221
(Gag Jirak)

757
46:23.291 --> 46:24.461
Welcome.

758
46:32.501 --> 46:34.001
An iced Americano, please.

759
46:39.771 --> 46:41.681
Tae Gu? He has not been here.

760
46:42.141 --> 46:44.081
Did he run away from home because he was upset?

761
46:44.211 --> 46:46.581
You know he is not the type to do that over a cancelled taping.

762
46:46.951 --> 46:48.981
What is it? Did you guys fight?

763
46:49.351 --> 46:50.351
Of course not.

764
46:51.391 --> 46:53.221
If Tae Gu comes by, please give me a call.

765
46:54.961 --> 46:56.391
You totally fought.

766
46:57.261 --> 46:58.261
Hello.

767
47:00.431 --> 47:02.301
Sighing while saying, "Of course not"...

768
47:02.361 --> 47:04.131
means you definitely had a fight, right?

769
47:05.231 --> 47:07.471
You do not seem like the type to pick a fight, though.

770
47:07.871 --> 47:10.041
It was Tae Gu and Nam Il who fought, wasn't it?

771
47:14.981 --> 47:15.981
Are we close?

772
47:16.241 --> 47:17.251
Excuse me?

773
47:20.581 --> 47:24.351
Okay, message received. Pardon my intrusion.

774
47:27.991 --> 47:29.061
Hyun Woo.

775
47:29.421 --> 47:30.931
Is Tae Gu at the theater by any chance?

776
47:30.991 --> 47:32.331
I thought he was a gentle guy,

777
47:32.391 --> 47:33.961
but he actually has some sharp thorns.

778
47:34.701 --> 47:35.701
It stings.

779
47:35.861 --> 47:37.431
Sorry to bother you, but could you check for me?

780
47:39.201 --> 47:40.201
Yes, thanks.

781
47:43.941 --> 47:44.971
They fought?

782
47:45.171 --> 47:47.881
Yes. Jun Seo said no, but you know my intuition, right?

783
47:48.181 --> 47:49.181
I'm one hundred percent sure.

784
47:49.381 --> 47:51.811
And apparently, their taping got cancelled.

785
47:51.881 --> 47:53.681
- What? - Shocking, right?

786
47:53.881 --> 47:55.781
Those network people are so heartless, aren't they?

787
47:56.421 --> 47:57.421
Eun Young.

788
47:59.221 --> 48:00.221
Yes?

789
48:01.491 --> 48:02.721
Should we start closing up?

790
48:06.431 --> 48:07.861
When is that jerk going to leave?

791
48:08.361 --> 48:11.531
- I will just kick him out. - Wait a moment.

792
48:12.471 --> 48:16.401
I have somewhere to be later. You guys go ahead and head out.

793
48:16.441 --> 48:17.971
I will close up.

794
48:19.811 --> 48:22.011
- Really? - All right, then.

795
48:22.281 --> 48:23.311
Thank you.

796
48:25.381 --> 48:26.451
Score.

797
49:15.561 --> 49:16.561
Excuse me.

798
49:20.571 --> 49:21.571
Excuse me.

799
49:42.661 --> 49:43.661
Excuse me.

800
49:52.001 --> 49:53.001
Excuse me.

801
50:12.791 --> 50:16.561
- Are you all done? - Yes. You were asleep, so...

802
50:17.761 --> 50:18.961
I was not sleeping...

803
50:19.661 --> 50:20.661
Pardon?

804
50:22.761 --> 50:23.801
Well...

805
50:24.371 --> 50:25.801
I put my cup over there.

806
50:26.401 --> 50:27.471
The pen is here.

807
50:32.841 --> 50:35.341
Oh, I came in to wake you up.

808
50:37.051 --> 50:39.011
Good night. I am sorry.

809
51:09.781 --> 51:10.911
When do you get off work?

810
51:44.311 --> 51:45.311
Bye, then.

811
51:55.261 --> 51:56.261
Hey.

812
52:01.061 --> 52:02.531
Aren't you going home?

813
52:03.701 --> 52:04.701
I'm not.

814
52:06.131 --> 52:08.541
Then why did you walk all the way here?

815
52:09.141 --> 52:10.371
You are late because of me.

816
52:11.641 --> 52:12.671
The streetlamp.

817
52:14.341 --> 52:15.441
It hasn't been fixed yet.

818
52:28.661 --> 52:29.921
Well...

819
52:34.801 --> 52:35.801
By any chance,

820
52:37.331 --> 52:39.201
are you hungry?

821
52:41.701 --> 52:42.701
Pardon?

822
52:46.971 --> 52:49.441
Ten years ago, when I left home to do comedy...

823
52:50.551 --> 52:51.881
and the three of us were house-hunting,

824
52:54.751 --> 52:56.451
there were plenty of places better than this.

825
52:59.521 --> 53:00.861
But that view,

826
53:02.821 --> 53:05.161
for that one single thing, we moved in here.

827
53:07.861 --> 53:09.201
Just looking at it felt so good.

828
53:18.471 --> 53:19.711
Don't you have anything like that?

829
53:23.281 --> 53:24.281
Something...

830
53:25.181 --> 53:26.981
no one else understands,

831
53:28.581 --> 53:29.651
but you love.

832
53:32.091 --> 53:33.451
Something you just can't live without.

833
53:47.901 --> 53:49.001
It is better not to have one.

834
53:50.711 --> 53:52.211
If you care about anything too deeply,

835
53:54.281 --> 53:55.541
it is bad for the heart.

836
54:06.791 --> 54:08.291
- I do. - You startled me.

837
54:09.391 --> 54:12.731
I have something like that too.

838
54:20.171 --> 54:21.241
Tough luck for you, then.

839
54:32.011 --> 54:34.951
Does it still hurt?

840
54:39.651 --> 54:40.661
Sometimes.

841
54:42.321 --> 54:43.621
Darn it.

842
54:44.891 --> 54:47.191
I wanted to catch and pay her back in kind.

843
54:48.161 --> 54:50.571
Did she notice? How come she hasn't shown up once?

844
54:53.871 --> 54:56.901
You must be really angry.

845
54:56.901 --> 54:59.741
Of course I am. My perfectly fine nose got broken.

846
55:01.841 --> 55:03.181
Whether it is a psycho or a maniac,

847
55:04.151 --> 55:05.411
once I catch her...

848
55:12.551 --> 55:13.591
I am going to ask.

849
55:18.761 --> 55:19.791
Ask her...

850
55:24.701 --> 55:26.171
what I am supposed to do.

851
55:28.871 --> 55:29.941
That person...

852
55:32.241 --> 55:33.711
has been watching us all this time,

853
55:36.411 --> 55:37.911
so I thought she might know.

854
55:47.151 --> 55:48.521
Because I really don't know.

855
55:52.631 --> 55:54.401
What the right thing to do is.

856
56:33.901 --> 56:35.901
Hey, it's been so long since we went to the countryside.

857
56:36.441 --> 56:38.941
Feels like a road trip, doesn't it?

858
56:43.551 --> 56:46.411
Nam Il, do you want some squid?

859
56:47.181 --> 56:49.551
This stone-grilled stuff is incredible.

860
56:49.621 --> 56:51.721
Nam Il, here, have one.

861
56:53.961 --> 56:55.321
Tell me if you want more. I will give you some.

862
56:57.261 --> 56:59.061
Are you sleepy?

863
56:59.291 --> 57:02.901
You must be tired. Want some gum?

864
57:03.501 --> 57:06.771
- Or chocolate? - Hold on.

865
57:08.171 --> 57:09.171
Here.

866
57:09.441 --> 57:10.441
Hello?

867
57:10.671 --> 57:13.211
Tae Gu. We need to push it back three hours.

868
57:14.711 --> 57:15.711
What?

869
57:15.781 --> 57:17.111
Sorry, that's just how it turned out.

870
57:17.481 --> 57:18.881
Why are you telling us this only now?

871
57:29.191 --> 57:32.091
It's fine. We can just wait there when we arrive.

872
57:32.861 --> 57:35.501
(Green Room)

873
57:36.031 --> 57:38.331
- MCs, please stand by right now. - Okay.

874
57:38.671 --> 57:40.131
Hello, we are...

875
57:40.241 --> 57:42.941
- Here to turn your mind... - Into total chaos.

876
57:43.201 --> 57:44.341
- We are Asura. - We are Asura.

877
57:44.971 --> 57:46.771
(14th Gangmasan Wild Herb Festival)

878
57:48.811 --> 57:50.911
- All right. - That's right.

879
57:50.981 --> 57:53.151
Yes, the weather is quite chilly today.

880
57:53.211 --> 57:54.481
Taking a shower was completely pointless.

881
57:54.621 --> 57:57.191
- Tell me about it. - Cut the nonsense...

882
57:57.251 --> 57:59.021
and do the raffle already!

883
57:59.091 --> 58:01.761
Isn't that what we're all waiting for?

884
58:01.961 --> 58:04.161
To all the folks waiting...

885
58:04.231 --> 58:07.031
The raffle is prepared for part two.

886
58:07.101 --> 58:08.661
- That is right. - Yes.

887
58:08.731 --> 58:10.331
- Nonsense! - Goodness.

888
58:10.871 --> 58:12.471
Thank you for the rice wine. We will enjoy it.

889
58:12.531 --> 58:13.671
Thank you for your sponsorship.

890
58:13.741 --> 58:15.441
- What's this? Hey, bastards. - You are full of energy, sir.

891
58:15.501 --> 58:17.711
- Overflowing with it. - And now, a surprise event...

892
58:17.771 --> 58:18.771
A surprise event!

893
58:19.341 --> 58:21.581
- Yes, congratulations. - Good work.

894
58:21.881 --> 58:23.411
- Thank you. - True professionals.

895
58:23.511 --> 58:25.911
Next up, it's valued at 100 dollars.

896
58:26.251 --> 58:29.951
Let us draw a ticket for an iron. Now, let us draw. Yes.

897
58:30.081 --> 58:32.821
Sir, not yet. All right, here we go.

898
58:33.121 --> 58:35.091
Excuse me.

899
58:35.961 --> 58:37.291
This is different from what we agreed on.

900
58:37.661 --> 58:38.661
Congratulations.

901
58:38.731 --> 58:40.361
Mi Jeong must have made another mistake.

902
58:41.601 --> 58:44.001
Fine, next time, I will give you extra, okay?

903
58:44.431 --> 58:46.501
Next up, for a vacuum cleaner...

904
58:46.501 --> 58:48.901
Last time, you shorted us 100 dollars the exact same way.

905
58:50.101 --> 58:51.111
Give it to us now.

906
58:51.771 --> 58:54.281
The lucky number for the vacuum cleaner...

907
58:55.011 --> 58:57.581
- is number 65. - Hey, what is wrong with you today?

908
58:58.151 --> 58:59.251
Asura!

909
58:59.311 --> 59:00.821
Hey, do you guys not want gigs anymore?

910
59:01.581 --> 59:03.021
Please come up to the front.

911
59:03.421 --> 59:04.591
Are you threatening us right now?

912
59:05.521 --> 59:09.891
You are indeed number 65, sir. Yes, you can take your prize.

913
59:09.961 --> 59:11.091
Pay us properly. Give us our money.

914
59:11.631 --> 59:12.931
Now, we will keep the raffle going.

915
59:12.991 --> 59:14.001
What do you think you're doing?

916
59:14.061 --> 59:16.131
- Give us our money! - Hey.

917
59:16.201 --> 59:18.271
- Hand it over, darn it. - Tae Gu.

918
59:18.331 --> 59:19.771
- Seriously. Darn it! - Stop it.

919
59:20.301 --> 59:21.341
- Hey, get over here. - Give it.

920
59:21.641 --> 59:23.201
- Hey! - Hit me, you punk.

921
59:23.201 --> 59:25.111
- Hey, hand it over. - Hit me, you punk.

922
59:25.171 --> 59:26.871
- Stop it, Tae Gu. - Hit me.

923
59:26.941 --> 59:28.011
I dare you to hit!

924
59:28.281 --> 59:29.311
Let go!

925
59:29.511 --> 59:32.451
I am telling you, he hit me first.

926
59:33.951 --> 59:34.951
Those...

927
59:35.781 --> 59:37.751
I felt sorry for those pathetic nobodies...

928
59:38.351 --> 59:41.091
and hired them, and they show zero gratitude.

929
59:41.161 --> 59:42.391
Keep it down, please.

930
59:43.421 --> 59:44.431
Name.

931
59:46.761 --> 59:47.761
Kang Tae Gu.

932
59:48.201 --> 59:49.201
Age?

933
59:49.501 --> 59:50.501
Thirty-four.

934
59:51.031 --> 59:52.031
Address?

935
59:52.401 --> 59:55.941
Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul, 82, Dangsan 9-dong.

936
59:57.641 --> 59:58.641
Occupation.

937
01:00:07.381 --> 01:00:08.381
Your occupation.

938
01:00:15.391 --> 01:00:18.531
(Gangma Rest Stop)

939
01:00:29.201 --> 01:00:30.201
That saved me.

940
01:00:40.421 --> 01:00:41.621
- Hey. - Yes?

941
01:00:41.621 --> 01:00:42.981
Look in the mirror.

942
01:00:43.021 --> 01:00:44.521
Does that look like someone who's saved?

943
01:00:44.721 --> 01:00:47.561
Hey, did you see him earlier with his chapped lips,

944
01:00:48.491 --> 01:00:49.521
eating like this?

945
01:00:49.921 --> 01:00:52.891
When did I ever eat like that?

946
01:00:53.591 --> 01:00:54.601
Stop exaggerating.

947
01:00:55.301 --> 01:00:56.301
What time is it?

948
01:00:57.371 --> 01:00:58.801
We ate really fast.

949
01:00:59.571 --> 01:01:00.571
It's a new record.

950
01:01:00.841 --> 01:01:02.541
I guess we were starving since it's our first meal.

951
01:01:05.611 --> 01:01:07.011
You're right, this was our first meal.

952
01:01:13.151 --> 01:01:15.351
- Let's go. - All right, let's go.

953
01:01:16.021 --> 01:01:17.451
I'll drive from here.

954
01:01:22.191 --> 01:01:23.191
Guys.

955
01:01:42.811 --> 01:01:43.881
Let's call it quits.

956
01:01:59.831 --> 01:02:01.261
Seriously, this guy...

957
01:02:02.861 --> 01:02:04.601
What a persistent jerk, really.

958
01:03:02.221 --> 01:03:03.391
Come to think of it,

959
01:03:03.391 --> 01:03:04.631
Three Iced Americanos haven't been by.

960
01:03:05.391 --> 01:03:08.701
Right. Did something happen? Not that I'm complaining.

961
01:03:11.201 --> 01:03:12.431
Why is it so dusty in here?

962
01:03:15.441 --> 01:03:20.711
- Long time no see, ladies. Hello. - Stop hitting on everyone, please.

963
01:03:20.781 --> 01:03:21.781
Seriously.

964
01:03:24.411 --> 01:03:26.181
Three iced Americanos, please.

965
01:03:34.991 --> 01:03:37.491
I have a gift for you.

966
01:03:45.471 --> 01:03:47.131
Goodness.

967
01:03:47.171 --> 01:03:50.871
You're going to hyperventilate. Are you that happy?

968
01:03:50.941 --> 01:03:54.211
These aren't just regular tickets. They're invitations.

969
01:03:54.741 --> 01:03:56.981
And Asura gave them to us personally.

970
01:03:58.151 --> 01:04:00.551
I'm so glad we ate with them that day.

971
01:04:01.881 --> 01:04:02.881
Thank you.

972
01:04:03.521 --> 01:04:05.691
Only now?

973
01:04:10.761 --> 01:04:12.261
Are you sure you'll be okay, though?

974
01:04:13.291 --> 01:04:14.961
You struggle with crowded places.

975
01:04:16.031 --> 01:04:17.131
Didn't you say you always went...

976
01:04:17.201 --> 01:04:18.431
all the way to the venue and turned back?

977
01:04:19.501 --> 01:04:20.531
I'm going.

978
01:04:21.441 --> 01:04:22.901
It's their tenth anniversary show.

979
01:04:24.641 --> 01:04:25.911
I really want to go.

980
01:04:26.971 --> 01:04:27.981
I have to.

981
01:04:28.941 --> 01:04:30.181
All right, let's go.

982
01:04:30.241 --> 01:04:32.211
(Tenth Anniversary Special Show)

983
01:04:32.281 --> 01:04:34.781
(The Perfect Cleaning Experts: Clean Team)

984
01:04:41.121 --> 01:04:42.121
Are you okay?

985
01:04:44.361 --> 01:04:45.361
Yes.

986
01:04:54.441 --> 01:04:56.901
- It's starting. - Whatever you imagine,

987
01:04:57.441 --> 01:04:59.041
you will see so much more.

988
01:04:59.471 --> 01:05:02.481
Introducing South Korea's greatest comedy trio.

989
01:05:03.111 --> 01:05:04.111
A...

990
01:05:04.751 --> 01:05:05.951
su...

991
01:05:06.851 --> 01:05:08.981
ra.

992
01:05:19.091 --> 01:05:21.631
- Hello, we are... - Here to turn your mind...

993
01:05:21.701 --> 01:05:23.061
Into total chaos.

994
01:05:23.961 --> 01:05:25.031
- We are Asura. - We are Asura.

995
01:05:26.801 --> 01:05:29.571
It's already so funny!

996
01:05:32.971 --> 01:05:34.711
First of all, to everyone who came...

997
01:05:34.781 --> 01:05:35.941
to our tenth anniversary opening show,

998
01:05:36.011 --> 01:05:37.211
we are endlessly grateful.

999
01:05:37.681 --> 01:05:41.051
Before we begin our performance, we have an announcement to make.

1000
01:05:41.751 --> 01:05:43.121
This tenth anniversary run...

1001
01:05:43.181 --> 01:05:44.951
is scheduled for a total of ten shows.

1002
01:05:45.591 --> 01:05:49.261
After we give our very best to complete these ten performances,

1003
01:05:59.631 --> 01:06:00.771
Asura will be disbanding.

1004
01:06:01.871 --> 01:06:03.601
- What? - What?

1005
01:06:03.901 --> 01:06:04.911
Why?

1006
01:06:04.971 --> 01:06:06.571
Did he just say they are disbanding?

1007
01:06:08.011 --> 01:06:09.411
They must not be making any money.

1008
01:06:10.411 --> 01:06:11.411
Oh, no.

1009
01:06:50.221 --> 01:06:52.091
They always acted so bright and cheerful,

1010
01:06:53.321 --> 01:06:55.391
but I guess even they reached their limit.

1011
01:07:03.601 --> 01:07:04.731
Que sera, sera.

1012
01:07:07.271 --> 01:07:08.701
Whatever will be, will be.

1013
01:07:10.701 --> 01:07:11.871
Yet, destiny can be...

1014
01:07:12.671 --> 01:07:14.781
as cruel as it is beautiful,

1015
01:07:15.341 --> 01:07:18.851
and some endings bring failure and despair.

1016
01:07:20.281 --> 01:07:21.351
However,

1017
01:07:22.021 --> 01:07:25.351
if you can overcome that despair on your own...

1018
01:07:25.721 --> 01:07:27.861
and find the courage to step outside your destiny,

1019
01:07:30.021 --> 01:07:33.861
it is at that exact moment that destiny grants a new hope.

1020
01:07:39.031 --> 01:07:41.771
What is it? What's wrong? Eun Young!

1021
01:08:02.391 --> 01:08:04.531
- Gosh! - Gosh, you scared me!

1022
01:08:05.461 --> 01:08:06.461
- What is this? - What is this?

1023
01:08:06.831 --> 01:08:07.831
What is going on?

1024
01:08:08.401 --> 01:08:09.401
What is she doing?

1025
01:08:11.071 --> 01:08:12.071
Darn it.

1026
01:08:12.131 --> 01:08:14.701
Hey, stop. Don't go. Who knows what she might do?

1027
01:08:14.771 --> 01:08:16.371
- Hey. - Hey.

1028
01:08:23.341 --> 01:08:24.451
I am...

1029
01:08:25.751 --> 01:08:27.211
that crazy girl.

1030
01:08:51.641 --> 01:08:52.871
I am...

1031
01:08:54.441 --> 01:08:56.081
your fan.

1032
01:08:57.911 --> 01:08:59.251
So please,

1033
01:09:02.051 --> 01:09:03.351
don't disband.

1034
01:09:07.091 --> 01:09:08.661
You can't.

1035
01:09:09.561 --> 01:09:10.661
You can't disband.

1036
01:09:38.591 --> 01:09:40.351
It is at that exact moment...

1037
01:09:41.091 --> 01:09:42.991
that destiny grants a new hope.

1038
01:09:46.831 --> 01:09:50.561
(Happy Anding)

1039
01:09:50.971 --> 01:09:52.431
There really was someone.

1040
01:09:52.631 --> 01:09:55.841
- Someone who told us not to quit. - Is this how stars feel...

1041
01:09:55.901 --> 01:09:57.911
- when they have a die-hard fan? - Please.

1042
01:09:58.141 --> 01:09:59.141
Could you reconsider, just once?

1043
01:09:59.641 --> 01:10:01.911
No.

1044
01:10:02.881 --> 01:10:03.881
We won't.

1045
01:10:04.481 --> 01:10:06.081
Our list of things to wrap up:...

1046
01:10:06.151 --> 01:10:07.721
the car, the place... we have to clear it all out.

1047
01:10:07.921 --> 01:10:11.191
I'll start a fan club, and I'll work hard.

1048
01:10:11.251 --> 01:10:12.921
No, I'll do a great job.

1049
01:10:13.391 --> 01:10:14.621
That's not cheering them on.

1050
01:10:14.691 --> 01:10:17.421
- That's just harassing them. - What are you doing?

1051
01:10:17.491 --> 01:10:19.691
- You're throwing that away too? - It's been ten years.

1052
01:10:19.761 --> 01:10:21.901
These are things we cherished...

1053
01:10:21.961 --> 01:10:23.301
and built together over ten whole years.

1054
01:10:23.661 --> 01:10:25.131
I'm not going to give up.

1055
01:10:25.201 --> 01:10:27.701
You must think I'm a pushover just because I hear you out.

1056
01:10:28.901 --> 01:10:30.071
I like you.

1057
01:10:30.141 --> 01:10:31.211
(Generative AI Used In Select Scenes)
